#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# unit_vector

#% text
# `unit_vector(n, k)` gives the vector of length `n` with a 1 at position `k` and 0 elsewhere; `unit_vector(k)` gives the 2-vector for `k` = 1 or 2.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The vector is the k-th column of `identity_matrix(n)`.

#% item
# `unit_vector(k)` is defined only for `k` equal to 1 or 2.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
unit_vector(4, 2)
#% output
#= [0, 1, 0, 0]

#% cell
unit_vector(2)
#% output
#= [0, 1]

#% cell
unit_vector(3, 3)
#% output
#= [0, 0, 1]

#% cell
dot(unit_vector(3, 1), [7, 8, 9])
#% output
#= 7

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `identity_matrix`, `diagonal_matrix`, `constant_array`
